course: dictionary
lesson: 6571
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «Grandad pulled on his nightcap and climbed into bed.» Pulled on and into bed tell you a nightcap is something you wear, so here it is a soft cap for the head.
explain: Now read this: «Mum brought me a warm milk as my nightcap.» The words warm milk and bed tell you that a nightcap can also be a drink. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Cosy words make things sound warm and comfortable. The words «a nightcap» are a cosy way to say a drink taken just before bed. Grown-ups sometimes mean a drink with alcohol in it, but for a child a nightcap is usually a warm milky drink.
fact: A nightcap can mean a soft cloth cap worn in bed to keep your head warm.
fact: A nightcap can also mean a drink taken just before going to bed.
fact: For children, a nightcap is often a warm milky drink.
fact: In old stories and fairy tales, characters like Scrooge and Wee Willie Winkie wear nightcaps.
exercise: «Grandad pulled on his nightcap and climbed into bed.» What is the nightcap here? | A tall hat for the rain | A drink of orange juice at lunch | *A soft cap worn in bed to keep the head warm | A bag for carrying your books
exercise: «Before bed, Ella had a warm milk as her nightcap.» What is a nightcap here? | A bedtime story | *A drink taken just before bed | Something you wear on your head | A soft pillow
exercise: Find the word in the lesson that is a cosy way to say a drink taken before bed. | warm | *nightcap | cosy | bedtime
test: «Sam wore a nightcap with a bobble on top.» What is the nightcap? | *A soft cap for the head in bed | A kind of sock | A cup of cocoa | A fancy restaurant
test: Why might a child's nightcap be a warm milky drink? | Because milk is the only drink in the world | Because nightcaps are always made of milk | *Because a nightcap can be a drink taken just before bed, and warm milk is a common choice | Because it is a sweet pudding
exam: In «Mum made me a warm milk nightcap before bed», what does nightcap mean? | A bedroom lamp | A warm bath | A soft cap for the head | *A drink taken just before bed
